{
  "what": "the k cells as first run, at the PRE-REGISTERED guidance batch size of 64",
  "why_kept": "k = 32 at batch 64 exhausts 24 GB: GPT-2 carries a full (key, value) KV cache, so repeating it 32-fold for 64 concurrent sequences is ~9 GB before the copy the repeat itself makes.  GP-MoLFormer's linear-attention cache is a running sum and does not grow this way, which is why configs/guidance.yaml could fix batch_size = 64 for every k and C31 cannot.  The sweep was re-run at batch 16 for EVERY k so that k remains the only thing that varies.  These rows are kept so a reader can check that the deviation moved nothing: the ComputeMeter charges `active` (not-done) sequences only, so the token accounting is batch-size independent by construction, and the sampling distribution per molecule is unchanged -- only the RNG draw differs.",
